# Tells Git which local, machine-generated, or secret files never belong in
# version control: the virtual environment, Python bytecode caches, tool
# caches, generated experiment outputs, and the real .env file holding API
# keys. It does not affect what gets published once a file is committed.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.env
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
# Exception: outputs/V1/ and outputs/V2/ hold only the real, audited runs
# that produced this project's reported results — V1's original 3x100
# baseline-network run (2026-08-03) and V2's nine-cell grid (2026-08-20).
# Both are committed on purpose so a fresh deploy of webapp/ (which has no
# persistent disk on a free host) always ships with real results, and so
# the raw traces behind the report's numbers are reviewable — see
# README.md's "Using the webapp" section. Every other outputs/ entry
# (calibration/smoke runs, older duplicate runs, anything a sandbox visitor
# generates) stays untracked.
!outputs/V1/
!outputs/V2/
.DS_Store